Package: ErythroWorkbench
Type: Package
Title: Sample Profiling for Erythrocyte Transcriptomics and Multi-Omics
Version: 4.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Kaicheng", family = "Shen", email = "kaichengshen2@qq.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Profiling the erythroid state of a sample before any modelling:
    how much of the signal is erythroid, how far a unit has drifted from fresh,
    where a sample sits on a maturation axis, which disease state its cells
    resemble, and which pathways are perturbed. All reference quantities are
    measured in house and shipped with the package, so scores reproduce the
    companion web server bit for bit. Scores are rank agreement with an in-house
    reference, not cell-count purity: mature red cells are enucleated.
